(4) In determining the maximum number of children to be specified under subsection (3) (a) of this section, the State Government shall take account of the number of other children who may at any time be on the premises (5) A State Government may at any time vary, remove or add to any of the conditions imposed under this section (6) The Minister may, by regulations, make provision as to conditions‐ (a) which shall be imposed by State Governments under this section in prescribed circumstances;
(b) of such descriptions as may be prescribed which shall not be imposed by State Governments under this section.
